<title>DENMARK: Danish Sept current account surplus 3.1 bln DKK.</title>
<headline>Danish Sept current account surplus 3.1 bln DKK.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1996-12-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Denmark's current account surplus stood at 3.1 billion crowns in September against a revised 1.9 billion crown surplus in August, the national statistics office said on Wednesday.  </p>
<p>DANISH CURRENT ACCOUNT (billions of crowns)</p>
<p>Figures for the past three, six and 12 month periods:</p>
<p>(Billions of crowns)  Three-month Six-month Twelve-month</p>
<p> Current account	     +5.7	   +9.8	  +10.0</p>
<p> Goods			   +10.8	  +21.7	 +39.3</p>
<p> Services			+2.6	   +5.6	  +7.4</p>
<p> Interest, other	     -7.6	   -17.5	 -36.7</p>
<p>NOTE - Figures are subject to rounding. Market analysts polled by Reuters had predicted an average September current account surplus of 3.3 billion crowns.</p>
<p>--Chris Follett, Copenhagen newsroom +45-33-969650</p>
